id: pm-pwq0g5
title: "The public harness detectors default env to an empty object, so detectAgentIdentity() and detectHarnessIdentity() silently return empty for every SDK caller"
description: "src/core/shared/author.ts:438 reads 'const env = signals.env ?? {}', so the two public detectors evaluate every descriptor against a zero-key environment when called with no arguments. Verified live: CLAUDECODE=1 is set and detectAgentIdentity() still returns {}. The CLI is unaffected because resolveAuthorIdentity routes through effectiveHarnessDetectionSignals, which supplies process.env."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",extensibility,identity,silent-failure
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:25:57.996Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T18:29:13.079Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "detectAgentIdentity() called with no arguments inside a known harness returns that harness rather than an empty object; The injected-signals path used by tests continues to work unchanged, including the AsyncLocalStorage seam; detectAgentIdentity and detectHarnessIdentity are documented in docs/SDK.md with the environment-resolution contract stated explicitly"
goal: project management = context management
value: "Makes automatic identity detection actually reachable from the SDK, which is the precondition for packages that adapt behaviour per harness."
impact: "Any package gating on harness identity degrades to its no-harness branch on every host with no error, no warning, and no telemetry."
outcome: "The public detectors resolve the ambient environment by default, or require the parameter so omission is a compile error; the symbols are documented in docs/SDK.md."
why_now: "Harness identity is the seam the project is actively investing in, and the one entry point an extension author would call is the one that cannot work."
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
dependencies[4]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind}:
  pm-03pq3o,implements,"2026-07-26T18:29:12.868Z",null,null
  pm-0zcwz6,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:12.868Z",null,null
  pm-itsjf0,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:12.868Z",null,null
  pm-w7mqzt,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:12.868Z",null,null
body: "## Problem\n\n`detectAgentIdentity(signals = {})` and `detectHarnessIdentity(signals = {})`\nare public SDK exports. Both are documented as pure detectors. Called the way\ntheir signature invites — with no arguments — they always return empty,\nbecause src/core/shared/author.ts:438 reads:\n\n```ts\nconst env = signals.env ?? {};\n```\n\nThe default is an **empty environment**, not `process.env`. Every descriptor\nmatch is then evaluated against zero environment keys, so no harness can ever\nmatch.\n\n## Live proof (2026-07-26, inside a real Claude Code session)\n\n```\n$ echo $CLAUDECODE\n1\n$ node -e 'import(\"./dist/core/shared/author.js\").then(m =>\n    console.log(JSON.stringify(m.detectAgentIdentity())))'\n{}\n```\n\nCLAUDECODE=1 is set and is exactly the key the claude-code descriptor lists in\n`environment_keys` (author.ts:97). Detection still returns `{}`.\n\nThe CLI is unaffected because it does not use this path: `resolveAuthorIdentity`\ngoes through `effectiveHarnessDetectionSignals` (author.ts:287), which supplies\n`{ env: process.env, ... }`. That is why real history entries do carry\n`author: harness:claude-code` / `author_source: detected`. The bug is confined\nto — and fully covers — the two functions an extension author would actually\nreach for.\n\n## Why this matters for extensibility\n\n- Both symbols are exported from src/sdk/index.ts (lines 33-34) and again from\n  src/sdk/core.ts (lines 107-108), so they are surfaced twice on the public SDK.\n- Neither appears anywhere in docs/SDK.md, so there is no documentation that\n  tells an author to pass `{ env: process.env }`.\n- The failure is silent: `detectHarnessIdentity()` returns `undefined`, which\n  is indistinguishable from \"no known harness\". A package that gates behaviour\n  on harness identity degrades to its no-harness branch forever, on every host,\n  with no error, no warning, and no telemetry.\n\nThis is the same seam class as the other identity defects: a correct primitive\nexists, but the consumer-facing entry point cannot reach it.\n\n## Direction (not a mandate for the fix)\n\nEither default `signals.env` to `process.env` in the public detectors (keeping\nthe injected-signals path for tests, which is what the AsyncLocalStorage seam\nalready provides), or make the parameter required so the omission is a compile\nerror rather than a silent empty result. Whichever is chosen, add the symbol to\ndocs/SDK.md — it is currently undocumented in both directions.\n\n## Relationship to the other identity items\n\n- pm-0zcwz6 owns model capture being inert (field exists, key list wrong).\n- pm-itsjf0 owns provenance being a fixed three-dimension schema\n  (CLAUDE_EFFORT=xhigh has no field to hold it).\n- This item owns the **public detector entry point returning empty**, which is\n  upstream of both and is a distinct defect: even a correct descriptor set and\n  a correct history schema would still be unreachable through the SDK API."
